atherClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503, making at most 3 requests in total. I checked it against a real local HTTP server and it behaved as intended in every case I tried.\n\n**How it works:**\n- If a request gets a 503 and attempts remain, the client waits `backoff * 2**attempt` seconds and tries again. With the default of 0.5, that's a 0.5s wait and then a 1s wait.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, the original `HTTPError` is raised to the caller.\n- Other HTTP errors (500, 404, etc.) are raised straight away with no retry. Network errors and timeouts are also not retried, because you only asked about 503.\n- There's a new `backoff=0.5` argument on the constructor, so tests or callers can shorten the waits. The attempt limit is a class attribute, `max_attempts = 3`.\n\n**Test results** (run with `backoff=0.05`):\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made | Waits between requests |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | JSON returned | 3 | 0.05s, 0.1s |\n| 503, 503, 503 | `HTTPError 503` raised | 3 | 0.05s, 0.1s |\n| 500 | `HTTPError 500` raised | 1 | none |\n| 200 | JSON returned | 1 | none |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add a test file. The check above was an ad-hoc run.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 70453, "requests_cache_write": 108773, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5953636, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1868, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial26", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 110, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:52:15.637795+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 22.276, "t_checker_s": 1.929, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netc